# Documentation Management

## Purpose

This center is a **general-purpose documentation management** namespace. Specialized
centers **may consume** its rules, missions, and skills for organization-specific
flows. Missions here can run end-to-end; agents **must ask** the user for details
that inform mission and lane skills (paths, remotes, conflict choices, org policy).

## Objectives

1. **Synchronize** local and remote documentation folders.
2. **Resolve** synchronization conflicts via the center's dedicated
   **conflict-resolution skill** (shared by all missions and agent lanes when present).
   Do not embed per-folder conflict policy in the registry YAML.

## Primary tool

**`rclone`** is the primary tool for synchronizing a local documentation folder
with its remote. Install and verify required tools (including `rclone`) via the
**Required Tools Installation** mission (`missions/required-tools-installation/`,
command phrase **`install required tools`**). The normative tool inventory —
minimum versions, docs/install URLs, OS method ids, and dry-runs — lives in
**`rules/10_required-tools.mdc`**. Do not invent an alternate sync engine unless a
later rule or mission explicitly authorizes it.

## Configuration file

Folder registry lives at the **hosting-repo root**:

```text
.sedea/documentation-management.yaml
```

- One or more **top-level documentation folders** are registered here.
- Each top-level folder has a **`slug`** (kebab-case) that keys its detailed config.
- Each folder has its **own rclone remote configuration** (remote name + remote path).
- Documentation folder contents are **gitignored** in the hosting repo — persistence
  is the remote/cloud store, not hosting-repo git.
- Because they are gitignored, each registered **`localPath`** **must** be
  force-included for Cursor SDK indexing via hosting-repo **`.cursorignore`**
  negations — see **§ Indexing force-include (binding)**.

### Schema (normative)

```yaml
version: "1"
folders:
  <slug>:                          # kebab-case top-level folder id
    localPath: <path>              # path under hosting workspace (gitignored)
    rclone:
      remote: <rclone-remote-name> # must exist in rclone config after setup
      remotePath: <path-on-remote> # path within that remote
```

| Field | Required | Rule |
|-------|----------|------|
| `version` | yes | Currently `"1"` |
| `folders` | yes | Map keyed by top-level **`slug`** |
| `folders.<slug>.localPath` | yes | Local tree root for that folder; gitignored |
| `folders.<slug>.rclone.remote` | yes | rclone remote name for this folder |
| `folders.<slug>.rclone.remotePath` | yes | Path on that remote |

**Forbidden:** inventing a second registry path; treating unregistered directories as
in-scope; committing documentation payloads into hosting-repo git; adding
`conflictPolicy` (or equivalent) to this registry — conflict handling belongs to
the shared conflict-resolution skill.

## Indexing force-include (binding)

Documentation payloads are **`.gitignore`d**, and Cursor SDK indexing honors
**`.gitignore`** — so by default agents **cannot** read or index these files, which
would make Documentation Management missions fail. To keep the folders indexed while
their contents stay out of git, the hosting repo carries a **`.cursorignore`** at its
root that **re-includes** each registered folder via negation lines.

**Contract (normative):**

- **`.cursorignore`** lives at the **hosting-repo root** (same level as **`.gitignore`**)
  and is **tracked** in git.
- For every registered folder’s repo-relative **`localPath`**, **`.cursorignore`**
  **must** contain both negation lines so the folder tree is indexed despite the
  **`.gitignore`** exclusion:

```gitignore
# Documentation Management — force-include indexed doc folder: <slug>
!<relativeLocalPath>/
!<relativeLocalPath>/**
```

- The force-include is authored in the **same** hosting **`WORKTREE_ROOT`**, in the
  **same** promote pass, and merged to **`main`** together with the **`.gitignore`**
  entry and the registry row — never as a separate worktree, PR, or follow-up.
- Writes are **idempotent**: do not duplicate lines already present for a
  **`localPath`**. Create **`.cursorignore`** with a short header comment if missing.

**Forbidden:** adding a **`.gitignore`** entry for a registered folder without the
matching **`.cursorignore`** force-include; treating indexing inclusion as optional,
best-effort, host-UI-only, or “sniff if present”; placing the force-include only in
chat, skills, or Sedea settings instead of the tracked **`.cursorignore`**; using
**`.cursorindexingignore`** or ad-hoc mechanisms in place of the negation lines.

## Rule numbering (this center)

Center rules under **`rules/`** use **two-digit** numeric prefixes stepped by **10**
(`00`, `10`, `20`, …) so new rules can insert at intermediate indices without
renumbering.

## Agent obligations

1. Resolve active folder(s) from **`.sedea/documentation-management.yaml`** — do not
   guess slugs or remotes.
2. When config, remote, or a sync/conflict choice is missing, **ask** via structured
   choice (or the mission skill’s gates) before mutating files or running sync.
3. When a conflict-resolution skill exists under this center, **use it** for sync
   conflicts — do not improvise a one-off conflict policy in chat.
4. When registering or **`.gitignore`**-ing a documentation **`localPath`**, also
   maintain the matching hosting-repo **`.cursorignore`** force-include negations for
   that path (**§ Indexing force-include (binding)**) — in the same tracked edit set.
   Never treat indexing inclusion as optional or defer it to a separate ship.
5. Prefer mission skills under this center for setup and sync; specialized centers
   that reuse these assets keep this contract unless they document a deliberate override.

